---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <header>
    <h1>Andrew Damanik</h1>
    <p>
      Junior at Arizona State University studying Applied Business and
      Technology Solutions
    </p>
    <a href="#contact">Get in touch!</a>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="about">
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Andrew! I'm a junior at Arizona State University studying
        Applied Business and Technology Solutions, and I'm interested in product
        management, AI/ML, and business analytics. I co-founded Kopi Deo, a
        restaurant in Jakarta, where I use customer feedback to improve our menu
        and dining experience. Outside of school and work, you'll find me
        producing music and DJing as SHIDEN, playing soccer, padel, or working
        on my golf game.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="projects">
      <h2>Projects</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>The Little House: Nonprofit website</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Role:</strong> Project Leader · Code the Change, Fall 2023
        </p>
        <p>
          A website for an education nonprofit in Indonesia that runs 4 schools
          for 200+ underprivileged children.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What I did:</strong> I co-led a team of 8 student developers from
          planning to delivery. I designed the Home, About, History, Gallery and Donate
          pages in Figma, split the build into tasks the team could take on, and ran
          weekly check-ins to clear blockers and keep us on schedule.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Built with:</strong> Figma, Python, Django, HTML, CSS, JavaScript
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/andrew415/Team1-Thelttlhouse"
          >View project</a
        >
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Freedom Wall: Student message board</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Role:</strong> UI/UX Designer · Google Developer Student Club, Fall
          2023
        </p>
        <p>
          A place for students to post and reply anonymously, after signing in
          with Google.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What I did:</strong> I designed the 4 core pages in Figma and mapped
          out how a student goes from signing in to making their first post, including
          every screen state for posting and replying. I worked directly with 3 developers
          to make sure the final Next.js app matched the designs on both desktop and
          mobile.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Built with:</strong> Figma, Next.js, React, Tailwind CSS, Firebase
          Auth
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>EcoHabits: Campus sustainability site</h3>
        <p><strong>Role:</strong> Developer · 2-day hackathon</p>
        <p>
          I noticed how many students at my school relied on plastic water
          bottles, so I mapped every place they could refill instead.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What I did:</strong> I walked campus, photographed 25 water fountains,
          and built an interactive Google Maps page with directions to each one. I
          also built the 4-page site around it, including a teammate's electricity
          bill calculator, and shipped it to GitHub Pages before the deadline.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Built with:</strong> HTML, W3.CSS, JavaScript, Google Maps API
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/andrew415/EcoHabits-Final4">View project</a>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Spotify Song Recommender</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Role:</strong> Data Engineer · Project Bracket, Fall 2023, 8-person
          team
        </p>
        <p>
          A music player that suggests songs similar to the ones already in your
          playlist.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What I did:</strong> I merged datasets with 586K+ tracks and 1.1M+
          artists in pandas, and pulled users' playlists through the Spotify API.
          That data fed the team's recommendation model, which matched songs by genre
          and popularity.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Built with:</strong> Python, pandas, Spotipy, Jupyter</p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Nxver-GitHub/ProjectBracket-AI-WebDev--Project-FA23"
          >View project</a
        >
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Facial Emotion Recognition</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Role:</strong> Data Acquisition · Project Bracket, 6-person team
        </p>
        <p>
          A model that reads facial expressions in real time and labels them as
          anger, fear, happiness or sadness.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What I did:</strong> I set up the data pipeline: organizing the
          workspace and the labeled image folders the model was trained on, using
          Python and OpenCV.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Built with:</strong> Python, OpenCV, TensorFlow (SSD MobileNet V2)
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:andrewhasintongan@gmail.com"
          >andrewhasintongan@gmail.com</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrew-damanik">LinkedIn</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/andrew415">GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>© 2026 Andrew Damanik</p>
  </footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  header,
  main,
  footer {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }
</style>
